# New files in packages are ignored by default, so nothing gets committed by
# accident: an app folder moved in can carry tokens, history or account
# details. Files git already tracks aren't affected. Add a new one on
# purpose, one file at a time (-f skips these rules, so never use it on a
# folder):
#
#   dots add -f common/.config/foo/foo.conf
#
# hooks/pre-commit is the backstop: it refuses paths in .secret-paths.

# Ignore every file...
*

# ...but not folders. With a folder ignored, `git add` on a tracked file in
# it still stages it, but warns and exits 1, so `dots add x && ...` stops.
!*/

# The repo's own files aren't config, so new ones show up as usual
!/.*
!/*.md
!/*.sh
!/hooks/*
!/LICENSES/*
!/profiles/*
!/tests/*

# Finder litter, wherever it lands
.DS_Store
